From 36d8d81faa5852ea7691308ef50de6691c6540f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:14:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 99/99] M-42, D-45, UX-37 and Beta desktop QA 4: the card's
 rounded range and the job page's exact one are the same range (P-2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Since fix-data-6's P-2 the job page states the posted figures exactly ("$60,200–128,800") where the card rounds them
("$60K–129K"). The four tests compared the two as strings. They now compare the currency and each figure rounded to the
card's precision, so a job page that shows one place's range under a card's span (the bug they guard) still fails.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014jaqot5Ddmi7Co6CofBiyc
